    "summary": "Hot '82 UC Davis show – scorching Let It Grow, seamless Scarlet>Fire, high‑energy jams",
    "review": "The March 14, 1982 gig at Recreation Hall in Davis captures the band in a fiery stride. From an opening One More Saturday Night that launches straight into a rolling set, the night builds to a blistering Let It Grow and a flawless Playin → Scarlet Begonias → Fire on the Mountain sequence that feels like pure telepathy. Jerry’s tone is crisp and his solos rip through the second set, while Brent Mydland adds fresh, soaring keys that lift tracks like Althea and Sugaree. Phil’s bass bombs on Sugar Magnolia and a heavy Not Fade Away keep the low end booming, and the Rhythm Devils unleash a tribal jam that showcases both drummers at their most inventive. The energy stays high throughout, rounding out with a rollicking U.S. Blues encore.\n\nMultiple soundboard sources confirm this is one of the cleaner ’82 recordings – the crystal‑clear board captured by Clugston (ID gd82-03-14.sbd.clugston.7220) presents every nuance without distraction, making it the go‑to version for anyone wanting to hear the band at full tilt on this night.",
